{"chunk_id": "305df87898fa", "text": "At Rama\u2019s great sacrificial gathering, sages, kings, monkeys, titans, and people of every rank assemble to witness a decisive moment: Sita\u2019s public oath of innocence. The immense crowd waits in tense silence until the sage Valmiki arrives, leading Sita. She walks behind him with bowed head and folded palms, overcome with grief yet inwardly fixed on Rama. The sight of the wronged queen moves the entire assembly to cries of sorrow and praise for both Rama and Sita. Valmiki then addresses Rama directly, declaring Sita\u2019s virtue and explaining that she had been abandoned near his hermitage because of public slander. He announces that she will prove her purity and reveals that the twin boys raised in his care are Rama\u2019s own sons. The scene prepares for a dramatic vindication of Sita before the whole world.\nValmiki brings Sita before Rama at the sacrifice assembly so she may publicly prove her innocence before sages, kings, and the gathered world.\nThemes: public vindication, honor and reputation, sage authority, Sita's purity, royal duty vs public opinion", "vector": [0.01149928942322731, -0.021607158705592155, -0.011559494771063328, 0.0002922485291492194, -0.02911280281841755, 0.016563257202506065, -0.02249017544090748, 0.003438414540141821, -0.028203027322888374, -0.02540680579841137, 0.01215486228466034, -0.0027376872021704912, 0.0044953590258955956, -0.0006296513020060956, -0.009900493547320366, -0.000678986543789506, 0.043134041130542755, 0.004729492589831352, 0.021580399945378304, -0.006154360715299845, -0.006833347491919994, -0.0007981436792761087, -0.01569361984729767, 0.022543691098690033, -0.009659670293331146, 0.007124341558665037, 0.023266158998012543, -0.028898736461997032, 0.03106614202260971, -0.02128606103360653, -0.02732001058757305, -0.015319006517529488, -0.006338322535157204, -0.01258299220353365, -0.024911781772971153, 0.0020921481773257256, -0.0026942051481455564, -0.010549376718699932, 0.016